{
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "header",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Psychology\n\nDomain hub: perception, attention, learning, memory, emotion, motivation, language, social cognition, development and therapy models.\n\n[[Psychology Map|Open the domain map]] - snapshot of 2026-09-25; the map's *In this folder* section is the live view.",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 2100,
			"height": 170,
			"color": "#4CC38A"
		},
		{
			"id": "g0",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Perception and attention",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 1218
		},
		{
			"id": "s0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Psychology - Perception and attention|Perception and attention index]]**",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 88,
			"color": "#B8A4FF"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Attention]]**\n*process* - 8 sources\n\nSelection, capacity limits, sustained attention and the evidence for separable attention systems.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 508,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"color": "#4CC38A"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Attention and executive function]]**\n*framework* - 6 sources\n\nAttention as selection and executive function as a family of separable control processes, with the measurement gap between tasks and everyday life.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 762,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#4CC38A"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Perception]]**\n*process* - 5 sources\n\nSensation and perception distinguished, psychophysical thresholds, and the constructive character of perceptual experience.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 1040,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"color": "#4CC38A"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Working memory]]**\n*process* - 5 sources\n\nHolding and manipulating information over seconds: capacity limits, executive control and measurement issues.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 1294,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"color": "#4CC38A"
		},
		{
			"id": "g1",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Learning and memory",
			"x": 420,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 1750
		},
		{
			"id": "s1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Psychology - Learning and memory|Learning and memory index]]**",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 88,
			"color": "#B8A4FF"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Decision-making]]**\n*process* - 6 sources\n\nJudgment under uncertainty: heuristics, biases, framing effects and their interpretation.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 508,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"color": "#4CC38A"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Episodic memory]]**\n*process* - 4 sources\n\nMemory for personally experienced events: encoding conditions, retrieval cues, and the reconstruction problem.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 762,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"color": "#4CC38A"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Learning and conditioning]]**\n*process* - 5 sources\n\nClassical, operant and observational learning as three routes to behaviour change, and how cognitive accounts absorbed conditioning paradigms.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 1016,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#4CC38A"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Memory processes]]**\n*process* - 4 sources\n\nEncoding, storage and retrieval across memory systems, the reconstructive nature of recall, and which practice manipulations actually work.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 1294,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#4CC38A"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_4",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Motivation and reward]]**\n*process* - 6 sources\n\nDrive, expectancy and value accounts of why behaviour persists, and how reward is measured.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 1572,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"color": "#4CC38A"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_5",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Procedural memory and habit]]**\n*process* - 7 sources\n\nSkill learning, habit formation and the shift from goal-directed to automatic control.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 1826,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"color": "#4CC38A"
		},
		{
			"id": "g2",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Emotion and social",
			"x": 840,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 1194
		},
		{
			"id": "s2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Psychology - Emotion and social|Emotion and social index]]**",
			"x": 870,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 88,
			"color": "#B8A4FF"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Emotion regulation]]**\n*framework* - 8 sources\n\nEmotion components and theories, common regulation strategies, and why self-report, physiology and behaviour diverge.",
			"x": 870,
			"y": 508,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"color": "#4CC38A"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Language]]**\n*process* - 4 sources\n\nLanguage structure, development and the classical localisation models with their modern qualifications.",
			"x": 870,
			"y": 762,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"color": "#4CC38A"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Personality models]]**\n*framework* - 7 sources\n\nTrait models, dimensional measurement and the debate about consistency across situations.",
			"x": 870,
			"y": 1016,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"color": "#4CC38A"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Social cognition]]**\n*framework* - 8 sources\n\nHow people perceive, interpret and reason about other minds, and the interpretive frameworks used to explain differences.",
			"x": 870,
			"y": 1270,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"color": "#4CC38A"
		},
		{
			"id": "g3",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Development and therapy",
			"x": 1260,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 988
		},
		{
			"id": "s3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Psychology - Development and therapy|Development and therapy index]]**",
			"x": 1290,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 88,
			"color": "#B8A4FF"
		},
		{
			"id": "t3_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[CBT and its evidence base]]**\n*framework* - 5 sources\n\nThe CBT model, its behavioural roots, how its effects are tested, and the design constraints that come with psychological treatments.",
			"x": 1290,
			"y": 508,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#4CC38A"
		},
		{
			"id": "t3_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Developmental perspectives and attachment]]**\n*framework* - 9 sources\n\nLifespan developmental theories, attachment concepts, and how early relationships are studied without over-reading them.",
			"x": 1290,
			"y": 786,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#4CC38A"
		},
		{
			"id": "t3_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Therapy models overview]]**\n*framework* - 3 sources\n\nThe main psychotherapy orientations, what each targets, and how their evidence is generated and compared.",
			"x": 1290,
			"y": 1064,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"color": "#4CC38A"
		},
		{
